> the derivative of (sin x)^2 with respect to x
  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)^2
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = 2sin(x)*cos(x)
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-14)
> the derivative of x^2 with respect to x
  ucas: it(x) = x^2
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = 2x
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> partial derivative of x^2 y wrt y
  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2*y
  ucas: diff it y
∂/∂y it = x^2
  holds wherever the formula is defined
  check: matches central differences at 100 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
> the second derivative of x^4 with respect to x
  ucas: it(x) = x^4
  ucas: diff it x 2
d/dx it = 4x^3
d²/dx² it = 12x^2
  holds for every real x
  check: each order matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> the gradient of x^2 + y^2 at (1, 2)
  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2 + y^2
  ucas: grad it at 1, 2
∇ it = (2x, 2y)
  ∂/∂x it = 2x
  ∂/∂y it = 2y
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 200 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
  at (x = 1, y = 2): (2, 4), |∇| = 4.472135955
> hessian of x^2 + 2xy + y^2
  note: read "xy" as x*y (both are variables here; name it to use it whole)
  ucas: it(x, y) = x^2 + 2*(x*y) + y^2
  ucas: hessian it
Hessian of it (row i, column j: ∂²/∂j∂i):
  [ 2   2 ]   ∂/∂x
  [ 2   2 ]   ∂/∂y
  det = 0
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 400 points (max relative difference 3e-13)
  symmetric (the mixed partials agree) at 100 of 100 sample pairs
> laplacian of x^2 + y^2 + z^2
  ucas: it(x, y, z) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2
  ucas: laplacian it
∇² it = 6
  ∂²/∂x² it = 2
  ∂²/∂y² it = 2
  ∂²/∂z² it = 2
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 600 points (max relative difference 4e-13)
> the wronskian of sin x, cos x
  ucas: wronskian sin(x), cos(x)
Wronskian matrix of sin(x), cos(x) (row k: the k-th derivatives wrt x)
  [ sin(x)   cos(x)  ]   the functions
  [ cos(x)   -sin(x) ]   d/dx
  W = det = -1
  (W equals the numeric determinant at all 200 sample points of [-10, 10])
  check: every entry matches central differences at 402 points (max relative difference 3e-15)
  linearly independent: W(-1/20) = -1 != 0, so the functions are independent on every interval containing x = -1/20
> dy/dx for x^2 + y^2 = 1
  ucas: implicit x^2 + y^2 = 1 for y wrt x
on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:
  dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y
  holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)
  check: matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)
> the derivative of |x| with respect to x
  ucas: it(x) = abs(x)
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = sign(x)
  holds for x != 0
    at x = 0 it has a corner (slope -1 from the left, 1 from the right)
    (points looked for in [-10, 10])
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 1e-15)
